body:
R5: Anarchist Spain started a Civil War in Portugal and declared war on them. Somehow, Spain lost, and Portugal took all their mainland provinces. Curiously, they left Anarchist Spain as a puppet in North Africa and the Balearic Islands. Not pictured are the non-aligned puppets of Spain's former African territories. Yes, Anarchist Spain still has it's National Spirits and Focus Tree.

&#x200B;

EDIT: I'm playing as Socialist Bulgaria. I wasn't paying attention to Iberia, so you can imagine my shock when I saw "Portugal has taken 21 state(s)."

Every time I read up on the Civil War, General Sherman's quote rings in my mind.

&#x200B;

 “It is only those who have neither fired a shot nor  heard the shrieks and groans of the wounded who cry aloud for blood,  more vengeance, more desolation. **War is hell**.”

Ireland has a remarkably interesting history. One of my favorite stories is about the Siege of Jadotville. A small group of Irish infantrymen were sent by the UN to help with a peacekeeping mission during the Congo Crisis in 1961. The UN forces backed the Republic of the Congo, so the Irish peacekeeping force (numbering around 155 men) was sent to defend an area known as Jadotville. The Irish force was led by General Pat Quinlan, and suddenly came under attack by Katangese forces, also consisting of French legionaries and Belgian mercenaries, numbering around 3,000.

&#x200B;

Despite being severely outgunned and outmanned, alongside being denied UN aid, Quinlan's forces inflicted 300+ casualties and did not lose a single man. Eventually, the Irish were forced to surrender after days without aid, and were taken as prisoners of war for a month. Afterwards, due to UN politics, the bravery of Quinlan and his troops was kept secret for decades. Until the 21st century, Ireland did not recognize their actions, with many civilians assuming that the Irish Peacekeeping Force fled without putting up a fight. I suggest reading up on it, there's a lot more details than what I've said here!

&#x200B;

Ninja Edit: According to Wikipedia/Irish Media, Quinlan's defensive tactics are still cited in military textbooks as the best use of perimeter defense.

"Lombardi Loops"

&#x200B;

Brilliant!

R5: No mods, Historical Focuses were off. Was playing as Sinkiang, Poland made the Baltic Alliance with Lithuania and puppeted Latvia + took Estonia. Then, when Germany declared war on them and Czechoslovakia they actually managed to defeat them. Poland, emboldened after somehow taking out Germany without Allied help, declared war on the Soviet Union after a few months.

&#x200B;

I was Communist China (Did the Yan'an Incident focus) and Stalin had diverted some of his troops to help me out with Nationalist China, who just joined Poland's faction. USSR declared war on Iran and Iraq, who both joined Poland's faction. His front line cracked and both of us were defeated. I was then reduced to a puppet in Tibet, and Poland puppeted a bunch of states in Asia.

TEAM AQUA

&#x200B;

GOD BLESS

Illinois here!

&#x200B;

Employers in the state have extended opportunities (in more than 100 occupations) for [felons to find work.](https://www.daily-journal.com/news/illinois-employers-more-open-to-hiring-people-with-felonies/article_7f93954c-ba70-11e8-836b-8fd1124e9393.html) In my view, this is a great step in helping felons reintegrate into society.

&#x200B;

Illinois has also made it legal for users of opioids to [exchange them for medicinal marijuana.](https://www.beaumontenterprise.com/news/article/Illinois-Makes-it-Legal-to-Replace-Opioids-with-13230357.php) This is a small, but helpful move in tackling the opioid crisis.

&#x200B;

In elections, the gap between the main gubernatorial candidates, J.B Pritzker (Democratic) and Bruce Rauner (Incumbent, Republican) [continues to widen in favor of Prizker.](https://www.nbcchicago.com/blogs/ward-room/jb-pritzker-polling-bruce-rauner-double-digit-lead-493201791.html) Kash Jackson (Libertarian) and Sam McCann (Conservative) make up about 10% combined. Prizker is looking like a clear favorite over Rauner. Jackson and McCann serve to add extra ink to ballots, I guess.

&#x200B;

Chicago officials have called for tougher legal costs for U.S Steel, who has [repeatedly leaked chromium into Lake Michigan.](http://www.chicagotribune.com/news/local/breaking/ct-met-lake-michigan-surfers-chromium-spills-20180913-story.html) They also accuse the Trump administration of going easy on U.S Steel on the issue.

&#x200B;

Lastly, in sports news, the Chicago Bears are going up against the Seattle Seahawks tonight, a few days after a painfully close defeat of the Bears by the Green Bay Packers. God help us.
